# Cross-platform line-ending & encoding policy.
# Doc: docs/wiki/17-line-endings-and-encoding.md (mirror of Perpetua-Tools/wiki/10, canonical)
#
# Default: normalize every text file to LF in the repository. This is what
# ends "file keeps getting modified on checkout" for good — the stored blob
# is identical no matter who commits it, on any OS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files must stay CRLF in the working tree — cmd.exe tokenizes on 0d0a (PR #108).
# Git stores normalized text; eol=crlf checks out CRLF. Mac/Linux agents: do not strip \r.
# Policy: bin/orama-system/skills/git-history-surgery/references/platform-line-endings-turf.md
*.cmd  text  eol=crlf
*.bat  text  eol=crlf
*.ps1  text  eol=crlf

# Binaries: never diff as text, never convert line endings.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
